.TH BAD-DECISIONS 1 "2026-09-28" "Bad Decisions 2.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bad-decisions \- deal, validate, import, and inspect Bad Decisions card packs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bad-decisions
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B bad-decisions pack
.RI {validate|export|import|init-registry|replace-local} ...
.br
.B bad-decisions consequences
.RI {report|tui|rebuild|purge} ...
.br
.B bad-decisions
.RI {serve|deploy|status|reload|stop|doctor} ...
.br
.B bad-decisions
.RI {deploy|rollback} " local" ...
.br
.B bad-decisions
.RI {setup|deploy|rotate-token|status} " aws" ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bad-decisions
is the command-line engine and service toolkit for portable card-deck packs. With no subcommand it deals an interactive round. It can also produce one-shot output, stream rounds, manage .carddeck archives, and inspect the local Consequences analytics database.
.PP
An omitted pack selector means every pack in the loaded registry. Set BAD_DECISIONS_PACK_DIR to use a custom registry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.BR --oneshot
Print one rendered round and exit.
.TP
.BR --rapid
Continuously print rendered rounds.
.TP
.BI "--delay " seconds
Delay between rapid rounds. Must be positive and finite.
.TP
.BI "--packs " ids
Comma-separated pack IDs for both card colors.
.TP
.BI "--prompt-packs " ids
Override the prompt-pack selector.
.TP
.BI "--answer-packs " ids
Override the answer-pack selector.
.TP
.BR --list-packs
List available packs and exit.
.SH PACK COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "pack validate " archive
Validate a .carddeck archive without changing disk.
.TP
.BI "pack export " "pack-id archive"
Export a registered pack to an archive.
.TP
\fBpack import\fR \fIarchive registry-dir\fR [\fB--remote\fR | \fB--index\fR] [\fB--pack\fR \fIid\fR]...
Import an archive into an absolute registry directory without overwriting an existing pack. With
.BR --remote ,
.I archive
is an HTTPS .carddeck URL; with
.BR --index ,
it is an HTTPS CardDeck catalog and each
.B --pack
selects one catalog pack. Everything is downloaded and validated before anything is installed, and a failed index import removes only the files it created.
.TP
.BI "pack init-registry " registry-dir
Initialize an empty absolute registry with the bundled packs. Do this before importing into a registry that BAD_DECISIONS_PACK_DIR will point at, since that registry replaces the bundled one.
.SH CONSEQUENCES COMMANDS
.TP
\fBconsequences report\fR [\fIdatabase\fR]
Print aggregate analytics as JSON. If database is omitted, use BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_DB or the installed release database.
.TP
\fBconsequences tui\fR [\fIdatabase\fR]
Open the read-only Textual dashboard. It provides dashboard, combination, prompt, and recent-draw views; press d, c, p, or r to switch views and q to quit. Textual is included in the core package.
.TP
.BI "consequences rebuild " database
Rebuild aggregate counters. Requires an explicit absolute database path.
.TP
\fBconsequences purge\fR \fIdatabase\fR \fB--retention-days\fR \fIdays\fR
Purge retained records and rebuild counters.
.SH SERVICE COMMANDS
These manage a systemd install on Linux.
.TP
.BI serve " [--host address] [--port port] [--workers n]"
Run the API in the foreground with uvicorn. The defaults are 127.0.0.1, 8000, and one worker.
.TP
.B deploy
Run the portable deploy.sh from a source checkout. Requires root; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
.TP
.B status
Show systemctl status for bad-decisions.service.
.TP
.BR reload ", " stop
Reload or stop bad-decisions.service. Require root.
.TP
.BI doctor " [--url url] [--expect-version version | --any-version] [--app-root path] [--min-free-mb n] [--timeout seconds]"
Check a running deployment without changing anything: /healthz reports the expected version (by default this command's), /v2/packs agrees with its pack count, /v2/round deals, /web/ serves, and /docs/ redirects stay within the public prefix. When APP_ROOT exists it also reports a pending activation request, unused staged files, and free disk space. Give the public base URL, including any prefix, with --url (default http://127.0.0.1:8000). Exits 1 if any check fails.
.SH LOCAL DEPLOYMENT COMMANDS
These talk to a root-owned activator installed once with sudo ./deploy.sh bootstrap-rootless; the caller must be in the deployment group. They refuse to run from inside APP_ROOT/current or APP_ROOT/releases: install the management command separately, for example with pipx. Only one request can be pending; a second is refused until the activator writes its result.
.TP
.BI "deploy local" " [--wheel path] [--requirements path] [--redeploy] [--allow-older] [--app-root path] [--timeout seconds]"
Deploy the installed version, so upgrading the management install (pipx upgrade bad-decisions or pip install --upgrade bad-decisions) and then running this command updates the server. It refuses to run when PyPI has a newer version than the installed command (pass --allow-older to deploy it anyway), and the activator refuses to reinstall the version that is already serving unless --redeploy is given. The activator also requires free space under APP_ROOT/releases (1 GiB by default) and, when bootstrapped with PACK_DIR, loads the live pack registry with the new release before switching to it. Interrupting the command does not cancel a request that was already submitted; the activator finishes it. The wheel is ./dist's matching build, --wheel, or else this version's wheel downloaded from PyPI and checked against its published SHA-256; the pinned requirements.lock ships with the package. On failure, the tail of APP_ROOT/activation/log.txt is printed. Stage them for a root-owned release activator previously installed with sudo ./deploy.sh bootstrap-rootless. This application-only update does not grant access to service definitions, nginx, secrets, or existing immutable releases.
.TP
.BI "pack replace-local" " old-pack-id url --new-id new-pack-id [--app-root path] [--timeout seconds]"
Replace one named pack in a rootless install's registry (enabled by bootstrap-rootless with PACK_DIR). The HTTPS CardDeck archive is downloaded within the usual limits, fully validated, and must declare new-pack-id. The activator publishes it without overwriting, retires old-pack-id, restarts, and restores the exact previous files unless /healthz and /v2/packs show the new id without the old one.
.TP
.BI "rollback local" " [release-id] [--app-root path] [--timeout seconds]"
Ask the same activator to switch back to the newest known-good release that is not current, or to release-id, with the rules of sudo ./deploy.sh rollback: a failed health check restores the serving release, and success drops newer entries from the good-releases watermark.
.SH AWS COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "setup aws" " [--profile name] [--region region] [--bootstrap] [--certificate-arn arn] [--domain-name name] [--hosted-zone-id id] [--allow-http]"
One-time, repeatable account preparation: create the ECR repository (keeping the newest 10 images) and the protected management capability if missing (an existing one is never rotated), bootstrap CDK if it has not been (or with --bootstrap), and merge settings into ~/.bad-decisions.env. Production HTTPS requires a certificate-matching domain. A Route 53 hosted zone is optional; external DNS providers use the emitted API Gateway CNAME target.
.TP
.BI "deploy aws" " [--image uri | --source directory] [--yes] [--capacity spot|on-demand] [--desired-count n] [--max-count n] [--certificate-arn arn] [--domain-name name] [--hosted-zone-id id] [--allow-http]"
Build and push an immutable ECR image of the installed version (unless --image is given), show the CDK diff, and deploy the complete packaged AWS application after confirmation (--yes skips the prompt and is required without a terminal). Domain flags and --capacity (default spot) are saved for later runs. A custom HTTPS domain is required unless --allow-http is explicitly selected for a disposable smoke test, which serves the generated API Gateway URL.
.TP
.B rotate-token aws
Replace the management capability in Secrets Manager, save it locally, and force a new ECS deployment so every task uses it.
.TP
.B status aws
Query the authenticated read-only AWS management status endpoint using the protected local credential.
.TP
\fBpack publish-aws\fR \fIarchive.carddeck\fR [\fB--no-reload\fR]
Validate and atomically publish an archive, runtime pack, and catalog record to the configured AWS deployment.
.TP
.B pack list-aws
Print the AWS CardDeck catalog as JSON.
.TP
.B pack seed-aws
Publish any missing bundled packs and restart the configured AWS service. Use this after infrastructure deployment succeeded but initial seeding failed.
.TP
.B consequences report aws
Print the private DynamoDB Consequences summary using the configured AWS identity.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PACK_DIR
Absolute registry directory that replaces the bundled packs.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_ROOT_PATH
Public path prefix when served behind a reverse proxy, for example /bad-decisions.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_LOG_LEVEL
DEBUG, INFO (default), WARNING, ERROR, or CRITICAL.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_DB
Absolute path to the Consequences SQLite database.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_RECORDING
Enable or disable server-side Consequences recording.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_FEEDBACK
Enable or disable voting while retaining server analytics.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_PUBLIC_STATS
Enable public combination summaries.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_RETENTION_DAYS
Days to retain Consequences records (default 90).
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_FEEDBACK_TTL_SECONDS
How long a draw can still be voted on (default seven days); may not exceed the retention period.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CONSEQUENCES_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS
SQLite busy timeout in milliseconds (default 250).
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_DIR
Absolute private directory for ephemeral per-room SQLite databases. All workers serving one deployment must share this local directory.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_ROOM_TTL_SECONDS
Room lifetime in seconds before its ephemeral database is deleted.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_HAND_SIZE
Number of private answers held by each participant.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_MINIMUM_PLAYERS
Minimum connected participants required before the Responsible Adult may start.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_DISCONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
Heartbeat grace period before a participant is marked away without deleting their room slot, hand, score, or submission.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_MAX_ROOMS
Live rooms the server will host at once (default 200); further room creation gets 503 too_many_rooms.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_MAX_PLAYERS
Players per room (default 12); further joins get 409 room_full.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_PEER_PRESSURE_MIN_FREE_MB
Free space the room directory must keep before a new room is created (default 256).
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE
Per-client limit, per worker, for room creation, joins, and feedback (default 30); excess requests get 429 with Retry-After.
.TP
.B BAD_DECISIONS_CORS_ORIGINS
Comma-separated exact origins (https://host[:port]) whose browser pages may call the API. Unset means no cross-origin access.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.bad-decisions.env
AWS settings and the protected management credential written by setup aws.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bad-decisions/consequences.sqlite3
Typical service database location.
.TP
.I APP_ROOT/releases/, APP_ROOT/current, APP_ROOT/good-releases
Immutable releases, the serving release, and the known-good rollback watermark (APP_ROOT defaults to /opt/bad-decisions).
.TP
.I APP_ROOT/incoming/, APP_ROOT/activation/
The rootless activator's staging inbox, and its request, result.json, and log.txt.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration or operational failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid request or domain error.
